  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Akil Bandu Shaikh vs The State Of Maharashtra on 18 September, 2019 Author: Revati Mohite Dere Bench: Revati Mohite Dere aba.1851 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1851 Of 2019 Akil Bandu Shaikh ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Vishal A. Patil for the Applicant Mr. S. S. Hulke, A.P.P for the Respondent-State Asi Mr. C. M. Gaikwad from Kasa Police Station, Palghar, is present Coram : Revati Mohite Dere, J. Wednesday, 18th September 2019 P.C. : 1 2 By this application, the applicant seeks pre-arrest bail i connection with C.R. No. 132 of 2019 registered with the Kasa Police Station, Palghar, for the alleged offences punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188, 34 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sections 26(2), 27, 23, 26(2)(4), 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act and Rules. 3",
    "facts": "2 By this application, the applicant seeks pre-arrest bail i connection with C.R. No. 132 of 2019 registered with the Kasa Police Station, Palghar, for the alleged offences punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188, 34 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sections 26(2), 27, 23, 26(2)(4), 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act and Rules. 3 Learned counsel for the applicant submits that according t prosecution, the applicant supplied prohibited food articles, namely, Pan Masala, Gutkha to the accused No.1, who was arrested by Kasa Police SQ Pathan Akil Bandu Shaikh vs The State Of Maharashtra on 18 September, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/164954718/ 1 ::: Uploaded on - 20/09/2019 ::: Downloaded on - 20/0 aba.185 Station on 31st July 2019, when the police raided the shop of accused No. 1 and found the said articles in his shop.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that no offence under Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is disclosed qua the applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that no offence under Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code is disclosed qua the applicant.",
